": 0.7, "evaluation_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "strict_mode": false, "include_reason": true}}]}, "{\"actual_output\": \"Sure!\\u202fCareer\\u202fPoint\\u202fUniversity (CPU) structures its academic offerings around both the\\u202fdisciplinary areas\\u202fyou can study and the\\u202flevels of study\\u202fyou can pursue.\\n\\nFirst, in terms of\\u202fdisciplines, CPU groups its programs into six broad streams.\\u202fYou\\u2019ll find options in Engineering\\u202f&\\u202fTechnology, which covers things like B.Tech degrees; Computer\\u202fApplications, which includes courses such as BCA with a focus on data science; Commerce\\u202f&\\u202fManagement, where you can do an MBA or related business degrees; Health\\u202f&\\u202fAllied\\u202fSciences for medical\\u2011related studies; Agriculture\\u202fScience, which spans topics like plant\\u2011stress adaptation and biotechnology; and Legal\\u202fStudies, for law degrees such as LLB.\\n\\nSecond, CPU offers those subjects across the full educational ladder.\\u202fAt the entry\\u2011level you can enroll in a\\u202fDiploma\\u202fprogram to build practical skills quickly.\\u202fThe traditional\\u202fUnder\\u2011Graduate\\u202ftrack lets you earn a bachelor\\u2019s degree and lay a strong foundation.\\u202fFor students who want a seamless progression, there are\\u202fIntegrated\\u202fprograms that combine undergraduate and postgraduate study.\\u202fIf you\\u2019re aiming for deeper specialization, the\\u202fPost\\u2011Graduate\\u202foptions (master\\u2019s degrees) are available, and finally, for research\\u2011oriented scholars, CPU provides\\u202fDoctoral\\u202fprograms that focus on research excellence.\\n\\nSo, in short, CPU\\u2019s academic catalogue spans a variety of fields\\u2014engineering, computer applications, commerce & management, health, agriculture, and law\\u2014delivered at diploma, undergraduate, integrated, postgraduate, and doctoral levels.\", \"context\": null, \"expected_output\": \"CPU lists Diploma,